      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "A sulfone-containing fluorinated compound showed brain/plasma ratios between 4.167 and 8.467 in mice, providing strong evidence that sulfone-bearing structures can have excellent BBB penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "An 18F-labeled benzamide with a basic piperidine showed good brain uptake in mice, supporting that 18F-labeled aromatic basic compounds similar to the query can cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved experimental analogues, including those sharing the DABCO motif, sulfone group, or 18F-labeled basic aromatic features, demonstrate meaningful CNS access in rodents or humans. The consistent supportive evidence outweighs the low Morgan similarities and any physicochemical concerns about the polar sulfone or basic DABCO, leading to a pass prediction.",
